{"type": "AssistantMessage", "content": [{"thinking": "Every MLP3 neuron puts about 93% of its output into the 27-dimensional logit subspace, which confirms that subspace is the right one to look at. The neurons don't map cleanly onto single tokens, though; they write mixtures, so clustering them won't identify tokens. I'm considering whether ICA on the neuron outputs could separate the underlying logit directions instead.\n\nI'm weighing whether ICA on the neuron outputs could recover the unembedding directions, though the assumption that the mixing coefficients are independent or sparse looks shaky. A more concrete option is the OV circuit of the copy head L3H3, which should map token-identity directions onto the logit subspace. I want to check its spectrum restricted to L, and how much of its output lands there, and compare with the other L3 heads.\n\n"}], "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "error": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4505, "cache_read_input_tokens": 141318, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 4505, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "message_id": "msg_011CggRr2beQtY2CD5sc1wif", "stop_reason": null, "session_id": "89056057-2a60-45f1-8bae-fdde8453a94c", "uuid": "e126353c-04b6-4d1f-951c-d9e468987d72"}
{"type": "AssistantMessage", "content": [{"text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nnp.set_printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True, linewidth=250)\nhd=64\ndef hm(l,name,j):\n    s=slice(j*hd,(j+1)*hd); return W[f'W_{name}.{l}'][s]\nUp,Sp,_=np.linalg.svd(W['W_proj.3']); L=Up[:,:27]\nfor l in [3,2]:\n    for j in range(6):\n        OV=W[f'W_o.{l}'][:,j*64:(j+1)*64]@(hm(l,'v',j)*W[f'ln1_w.{l}'])\n        fr=np.linalg.norm(L.T@OV)**2/np.linalg.norm(OV)**2\n        S=np.linalg.svd(L.T@OV,compute_uv=False)\n        print(f\"L{l}H{j}: frac of OV output in L = {fr:.3f}; svs of L^T OV: {S[:27]}\")\n# MLP2 output in L\nfor l in [2,1,0]:\n    Pj=W[f'W_proj.{l}']; print(f\"W_proj.{l} frac in L: {np.linalg.norm(L.T@Pj)**2/np.linalg.norm(Pj)**2:.3f}\")\n```"}], "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "error": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4505, "cache_read_input_tokens": 141318, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 4505, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "message_id": "msg_011CggRr2beQtY2CD5sc1wif", "stop_reason": null, "session_id": "89056057-2a60-45f1-8bae-fdde8453a94c", "uuid": "2b685646-cb01-422a-b13c-e6994517c285"}
